/-!
# Projective varieties, and divisors on smooth varieties

Let `k` be a field. This file collects two groups of standard facts.

*Projectivity.* A proper variety over `k` carrying an ample invertible sheaf is projective; a
`k`-morphism from a projective variety to a variety is a projective morphism; a variety with a
projective `k`-morphism to a projective variety is projective; and on a projective variety some
positive tensor power `L^{⊗ m}` of an ample invertible sheaf `L` is very ample, i.e.
`L^{⊗ m} ≅ ι^* 𝒪(1)` for a closed embedding `ι : X ↪ ℙᴺ_k` over `k`.

*Weil and Cartier divisors.* On a smooth variety every local ring is regular, hence a unique
factorization domain, and the Weil and Cartier pictures of divisors coincide. A prime divisor
`P` is an effective Cartier divisor: its ideal sheaf is locally generated by one regular function
`g`, whose germ at the generic point of `P` is a uniformizer and at the generic point of every
other prime divisor meeting the chart is a unit, so `g` is a local equation of `1 · P`. The Weil
divisor `[τ] = Σ v_P(τ) P` of a Cartier divisor `τ` is its cycle of codimension one, and on a
locally factorial variety the cycle map is bijective. A section of `𝒪_X(τ) ⊆ 𝓜_X` has one value
`φ ∈ K(X)` at every point, and `σ ↦ φ` identifies `𝒪_X(τ)` with `𝒪_X([τ]) ⊆ 𝒦_X`: both are cut
out by `ord_P(φ) + [τ]_P ≥ 0` along the prime divisors `P` meeting the open set. Every invertible
sheaf has local frames and so is a divisorial sheaf, and every `ℚ`-divisor is `ℚ`-Cartier.

The same argument works at a single point `P` whose local ring is factorial, for instance a
smooth point of a normal surface: the prime of a prime divisor `E` through `P` has height one in
`𝒪_{X,P}`, so it is principal, generated by the germ of a section `s`; the zero locus of `s`
contains only finitely many other points of coheight at most one, and removing the closures of
those that do not pass through `P` makes `s` a local equation of `E` near `P`. Local equations
add, so every Weil divisor has a local equation near `P`, and a `ℚ`-divisor does after clearing
denominators.

## Main results

* `MMP.Foundations.isProjectiveVariety_of_isAmple_and_isProjective_and_exists_isVeryAmple`:
  the four projectivity statements.
* `MMP.Mori.Divisor.cartier_weil_dictionary_of_isSmoothVariety`: on a smooth variety every Weil
  divisor is Cartier, the ideal of a prime divisor is locally generated by a local equation, the
  Weil divisor map on Cartier divisors is bijective with `𝒪_X([τ]) ≅ 𝒪_X(τ)`, every invertible
  sheaf is a divisorial sheaf, and every `ℚ`-divisor is `ℚ`-Cartier.
* `MMP.Mori.Divisor.exists_isLocalEquation_of_mem_smoothLocus`: near a smooth point of a normal
  surface every Weil divisor has a local equation, and every `ℚ`-divisor has a positive multiple
  which is an integral divisor with a local equation.

## Implementation notes

A variety is `AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety` applied to the structure morphism `X ↘ Spec k`; a
projective morphism is `AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjective` (Stacks Tag 01W8), ampleness is
`Stacks.Ample.IsAmple` and very ampleness `MMP.Intersection.IsVeryAmple`. The projectivity
statements are made for an invertible sheaf `L` rather than a Cartier divisor `D`; the case of a
divisor is `L = MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf D`. In the second statement the target is only
required to be a variety: the graph of `f` is a closed immersion into `X ×_k Y`, which is
projective over `Y`.

Weil divisors are `MMP.Mori.Divisor X`, Cartier divisors in the sense of `𝒦_X^*/𝒪_X^*` are
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.CartierDivisor`, with invertible sheaf `MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf`
and Weil divisor `AlgebraicGeometry.cartierWeilDivisor`. The instances that `X` is locally
Noetherian, quasi-compact and normal, consequences of the geometric hypotheses, are needed for
these objects to be defined. "Cartier near `P`" is stated in the stronger form that `D` has a
single local equation on a neighbourhood of `P` (`MMP.Mori.Divisor.IsLocalEquation`). Only the
factoriality of `𝒪_{X,P}` enters its proof; the surface hypothesis is the source's setting.

## References

* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KollarMori], Notation 0.4
* [R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic geometry*][Har77], II.4.9, II.6.11, II.6.16, II.7.6
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01W8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01W8)
-/

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace MMP.Foundations

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry in
/-- **Projectivity of varieties.** Over a field `k`:
(1) a proper variety with an ample invertible sheaf is projective;
(2) a `k`-morphism from a projective variety to a variety is projective;
(3) a variety with a projective `k`-morphism to a projective variety is projective;
(4) some positive tensor power of an ample invertible sheaf on a projective variety is very
ample. -/
@[mmp "lem_mmp_foundation_km_absolute_projectivity_package"]
public theorem isProjectiveVariety_of_isAmple_and_isProjective_and_exists_isVeryAmple
    (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    (∀ (X : Scheme.{u}) [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] [IsProperVariety k (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
        (L : X.Modules) [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L],
        Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L → IsProjectiveVariety k (X ↘ Spec (.of k))) ∧
    (∀ (X Y : Scheme.{u}) [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] [Y.Over (Spec (.of k))]
        [IsProjectiveVariety k (X ↘ Spec (.of k))] [IsVariety k (Y ↘ Spec (.of k))]
        (f : X ⟶ Y) [f.IsOver (Spec (.of k))], IsProjective f) ∧
    (∀ (X Y : Scheme.{u}) [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] [Y.Over (Spec (.of k))]
        [IsVariety k (X ↘ Spec (.of k))] [IsProjectiveVariety k (Y ↘ Spec (.of k))]
        (f : X ⟶ Y) [f.IsOver (Spec (.of k))],
        IsProjective f → IsProjectiveVariety k (X ↘ Spec (.of k))) ∧
    (∀ (X : Scheme.{u}) [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] [IsProjectiveVariety k (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
        (L : X.Modules) [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L],
        Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L →
          ∃ m : ℕ, 0 < m ∧
            MMP.Intersection.IsVeryAmple k (MMP.Intersection.Scheme.Modules.tensorPow L m)) := by
  refine ⟨fun X _ _ L _ hL => ?_, fun X Y _ _ hX _ f _ => ?_, fun X Y _ _ _ hY f _ hf => ?_,
    fun X _ _ L _ hL => ?_⟩
  · exact (isProjectiveVariety_iff_isProjectiveMorphism k _).2
      (AmpleTwistAcyclicity.isProjectiveMorphism_of_isAmple _ L hL)
  · have h := ((isProjectiveVariety_iff_isProjective' k (X ↘ Spec (.of k))).1 hX).2
    rw [← comp_over f (Spec (.of k))] at h
    exact h.of_comp f (Y ↘ Spec (.of k))
  · have h := hf.comp ((isProjectiveVariety_iff_isProjective' k (Y ↘ Spec (.of k))).1 hY).2
    rw [comp_over f (Spec (.of k))] at h
    exact (isProjectiveVariety_iff_isProjective k _).2 h
  · obtain ⟨d, hd, h⟩ :=
      RelativeSerreVanishing.exists_isClosedImmersion_projectiveSpaceOver_of_isAmple
        (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) L hL
    obtain ⟨n, i, hi, hover, ⟨e⟩⟩ := h d le_rfl
    exact ⟨d, hd, MMP.Resolution.Bridges.isVeryAmple_of_isClosedImmersion k _ _
      (MMP.Resolution.Bridges.nonempty_tensorPow_iso_tensorPowModule X L d).some n i hover e⟩

end MMP.Foundations

namespace MMP.Mori

section SmoothVariety

open TopologicalSpace Opposite

/-- The local ring at a smooth point of a scheme over a field is factorial. -/
private theorem uniqueFactorizationMonoid_stalk_of_mem_smoothLocus {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} {f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} {x : X} (hx : x ∈ smoothLocus f) :
    UniqueFactorizationMonoid (X.presheaf.stalk x) := by
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, hV⟩ := mem_smoothLocus_iff.1 hx
  haveI := isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_smooth_over_field (V.ι ≫ f) ⟨x, hxV⟩
  haveI := IsRegularLocalRing.uniqueFactorizationMonoid (V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk ⟨x, hxV⟩)
  exact MulEquiv.uniqueFactorizationMonoid
    (V.stalkIso ⟨x, hxV⟩).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.toMulEquiv inferInstance

/-- An ideal sheaf whose support misses the affine open `U` has the unit ideal on `U`. -/
private theorem ideal_eq_top_of_forall_notMem_support {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (U : X.affineOpens) (h : ∀ x ∈ U.1, x ∉ I.support) : I.ideal U = ⊤ := by
  by_contra hne
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hle⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal _ hne
  let p : Spec Γ(X, U.1) := ⟨m, hm.isPrime⟩
  have hxU : U.2.fromSpec p ∈ U.1 := by
    rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, ← U.2.range_fromSpec]
    exact ⟨p, rfl⟩
  apply h _ hxU
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem hxU]
  rintro _ ⟨s, rfl⟩
  simp only [Set.mem_iInter]
  intro hs hmem
  have : p ∈ U.2.fromSpec ⁻¹ᵁ X.basicOpen s := hmem
  rw [U.2.fromSpec_preimage_basicOpen] at this
  exact this (hle hs)

/-- Distinct prime divisors: the generic point of `E` lies in the support of `P` only if
`P = E`. -/
private theorem eq_of_genericPoint_mem_support {X : Scheme.{u}} {P E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X}
    (hE : E.genericPoint ∈ P.support) :
    P = E := by
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure] at hE
  have hle : E.genericPoint ≤ P.genericPoint := specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr hE
  by_contra hne
  have hlt : E.genericPoint < P.genericPoint := lt_of_le_not_ge hle fun h =>
    hne (AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.genericPoint_injective
      (Specializes.antisymm (show E.genericPoint ⤳ P.genericPoint from h)
        (show P.genericPoint ⤳ E.genericPoint from hle)).eq.symm)
  have h2 := Order.coheight_add_one_le hlt
  rw [MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.coheight_genericPoint,
    MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.coheight_genericPoint] at h2
  exact absurd h2 (by decide)

/-- The local-equation statement at a point in the support of an effective Cartier prime
divisor. -/
private theorem exists_affine_ideal_eq_span_isLocalEquation_of_mem {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)
    (hcart : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor P.idealSheaf) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ P.support) :
    ∃ U : X.affineOpens, x ∈ (U : X.Opens) ∧
      ∃ (g : Γ(X, U)) (φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ),
        (∀ (Z : irreducibleComponents X) (hZ : componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ (U : X.Opens)),
          (φ : RationalFunctions X) Z = X.presheaf.germ U _ hZ g) ∧
        Divisor.IsLocalEquation (Finsupp.single P 1) U φ ∧
        P.idealSheaf.ideal U = Ideal.span {g} := by
  classical
  haveI := P.integral
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hxW, f, hf, hspan⟩ :=
    Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor
      P.idealSheaf hcart x
  have hgerm : ∀ y (hy : y ∈ W), IdealSheafData.stalk P.idealSheaf y =
      Ideal.span {(X.presheaf.germ W y hy).hom f} := by
    intro y hy
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ P.idealSheaf y ⟨W, hW⟩ hy, hspan,
      Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  have hnzd : ∀ y (hy : y ∈ W), (X.presheaf.germ W y hy).hom f ∈
      nonZeroDivisors (X.presheaf.stalk y) := fun y hy =>
    Stacks.Divisors.germ_mem_nonZeroDivisors hW hf y hy
  let u : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents X, (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z))ˣ :=
    fun Z => if h : componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ W then
      (by
        letI := (RationalFunctions.isField_stalk X Z).toField
        exact (isUnit_iff_ne_zero.2 (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero (hnzd _ h))).unit)
      else 1
  let φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ := (RationalFunctions.unitsEquiv X).symm u
  have hφZ : ∀ (Z : irreducibleComponents X) (hZ : componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ W),
      (φ : RationalFunctions X) Z = (X.presheaf.germ W _ hZ).hom f := by
    intro Z hZ
    change ((u Z : (X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z))ˣ) :
      X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) = _
    simp only [u, dif_pos hZ]
    rfl
  refine ⟨⟨W, hW⟩, hxW, f, φ, hφZ, ?_, hspan⟩
  rintro E ⟨y, hyE, hyW⟩
  have hηW : E.genericPoint ∈ W := by
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure] at hyE
    exact (specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr hyE).mem_open W.isOpen hyW
  have key : E.toComponent.hom ((X.presheaf.germ W _ hηW).hom f) =
      (φ : RationalFunctions X) E.component := by
    rw [hφZ _ (E.specializes_genericPoint.mem_open W.isOpen hηW)]
    exact TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes_apply _ _ _ _
  by_cases hEP : P = E
  · subst hEP
    rw [DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_single_self]
    have hmem : P.genericPoint ∈ P.support := by
      rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure]
      exact subset_closure rfl
    have hprime : Prime ((X.presheaf.germ W _ hηW).hom f) := by
      rw [← Ideal.span_singleton_prime (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero (hnzd _ hηW)), ← hgerm _ hηW]
      obtain ⟨y', hy'⟩ : P.genericPoint ∈ Set.range P.idealSheaf.subschemeι := by
        rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
        exact hmem
      rw [← hy', ← Stacks.Divisors.kernel_stalkMap_subscheme_eq_idealStalk]
      exact RingHom.ker_isPrime _
    exact (P.ord_eq_one_of_irreducible hprime.irreducible key).symm
  · rw [DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_single_of_ne hEP]
    have htop := (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support
      P.idealSheaf _).2 fun h => hEP (eq_of_genericPoint_mem_support h)
    rw [hgerm _ hηW, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top] at htop
    exact (E.ord_eq_zero_of_isUnit htop key).symm

/-- Away from the support of `P`, the unit section is a local equation of `1 · P`. -/
private theorem exists_affine_ideal_eq_span_isLocalEquation_of_notMem {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∉ P.support) :
    ∃ U : X.affineOpens, x ∈ (U : X.Opens) ∧
      ∃ (g : Γ(X, U)) (φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ),
        (∀ (Z : irreducibleComponents X) (hZ : componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ (U : X.Opens)),
          (φ : RationalFunctions X) Z = X.presheaf.germ U _ hZ g) ∧
        Divisor.IsLocalEquation (Finsupp.single P 1) U φ ∧
        P.idealSheaf.ideal U = Ideal.span {g} := by
  have hopen : IsOpen (P.support)ᶜ := P.idealSheaf.support.isClosed.isOpen_compl
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, hVle⟩ := (Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens)
    (show x ∈ (⟨_, hopen⟩ : X.Opens) from hx)
  refine ⟨⟨V, hV⟩, hxV, 1, 1, fun Z hZ => by simp, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rintro E ⟨y, hyE, hyV⟩
    have hne : P ≠ E := by
      rintro rfl
      exact hVle hyV hyE
    rw [DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_single_of_ne hne]
    simp
  · rw [Ideal.span_singleton_one]
    exact ideal_eq_top_of_forall_notMem_support _ ⟨V, hV⟩ fun y hy => hVle hy

/-- On a smooth scheme the ideal of a prime divisor `P` is generated, on an affine
neighbourhood of each point, by a regular function which is a local equation of `1 · P`. -/
private theorem exists_affine_ideal_eq_span_isLocalEquation (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} {f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    (hsm : IsSmoothScheme f) (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (x : X) :
    ∃ U : X.affineOpens, x ∈ (U : X.Opens) ∧
      ∃ (g : Γ(X, U)) (φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ),
        (∀ (Z : irreducibleComponents X) (hZ : componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ (U : X.Opens)),
          (φ : RationalFunctions X) Z = X.presheaf.germ U _ hZ g) ∧
        Divisor.IsLocalEquation (Finsupp.single P 1) U φ ∧
        P.idealSheaf.ideal U = Ideal.span {g} := by
  haveI := P.integral
  by_cases hx : x ∈ P.support
  · exact exists_affine_ideal_eq_span_isLocalEquation_of_mem P
      (isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_codimension_one_of_uniqueFactorizationMonoid P.idealSheaf
        P.codimension_one fun _ _ => uniqueFactorizationMonoid_stalk_of_mem_smoothLocus
          (by rw [hsm]; trivial)) hx
  · exact exists_affine_ideal_eq_span_isLocalEquation_of_notMem P hx

section CartierWeil

open MMP.Intersection Order

/-- An order of `D` along a prime divisor `P` is the multiplicity `v_P(D)`. -/
private theorem cartierMultiplicity_eq_of_isOrderAlong {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] {D : X.CartierDivisor} {P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X} {N : ℤ}
    (h : IsOrderAlong D (primeDivisorSubvariety P) N) :
    cartierMultiplicity D (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.genericPoint P) = N := by
  unfold IsOrderAlong at h
  dsimp only [primeDivisorSubvariety_genericPoint] at h
  obtain ⟨a, b, ha, hb, ⟨g, hg, hgab⟩, la, lb, hla, hlb, hN⟩ := h
  rw [cartierMultiplicity_eq_ord_of_isLocalEquationAt hg, hN]
  have hcoh : coheight (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.genericPoint P) = 1 :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.coheight_genericPoint P
  have ha0 : a ≠ 0 := nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero ha
  have hb0 : b ≠ 0 := nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero hb
  have hbK : algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk _) X.functionField b ≠ 0 :=
    IsFractionRing.to_map_ne_zero_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors hb
  have key : totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField _ g *
      algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk _) X.functionField b =
      algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk _) X.functionField a := by
    have := congrArg (totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField _) hgab.2
    rw [map_mul, totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField_stalkToTotalQuotient,
      totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField_stalkToTotalQuotient] at this
    rwa [mul_comm]
  have hTg := totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField_ne_zero_of_isLocalEquationAt hg
  have hord := X.ord_mul (x := MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.genericPoint P) hTg hbK
  rw [key, ord_algebraMap_stalk _ hcoh a ha0, ord_algebraMap_stalk _ hcoh b hb0] at hord
  erw [hla, hlb, ENat.toNat_coe, ENat.toNat_coe] at hord
  omega

variable (k : Type u) [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}} [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] [IsIntegral X]
  [LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of k))] {n : ℕ} (hX : IsPureDimensional X n)

/-- On an integral scheme of pure dimension `n` locally of finite type over a field, the
`(n-1)`-dimensional subvarieties are the prime divisors. -/
private def codim1SubvarietyEquivPrimeDivisor :
    Codim1Subvariety X n ≃ MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X where
  toFun V := ⟨V.1.ideal, V.1.isIntegral, by
    rw [Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CodimensionOneDivisor.codimension_closureSingleton_eq_coheight]
    exact (subvarietyDim_add_one_eq_iff k hX V.1).1 V.2⟩
  invFun P := ⟨primeDivisorSubvariety P, (subvarietyDim_add_one_eq_iff k hX _).2
    (AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.coheight_genericPoint P)⟩
  left_inv V := rfl
  right_inv P := rfl

private theorem coe_codim1SubvarietyEquivPrimeDivisor_symm_apply (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) :
    ((codim1SubvarietyEquivPrimeDivisor k hX).symm P : Scheme.Subvariety X) =
      primeDivisorSubvariety P :=
  rfl

include hX in
/-- The Stacks Weil divisor of a Cartier divisor is its Lazarsfeld cycle, reindexed by prime
divisors. -/
private theorem weilDivisorEquivFinsupp_cartierWeilDivisor_eq [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [NoetherianSpace X] (τ : X.CartierDivisor) :
    letI : IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
    (weilDivisorEquivFinsupp (cartierWeilDivisor τ) : MMP.Mori.Divisor X) =
      Finsupp.equivMapDomain (codim1SubvarietyEquivPrimeDivisor k hX) (cycleMap hX τ) := by
  letI : IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
  refine Finsupp.ext fun P => ?_
  rw [Finsupp.equivMapDomain_apply, cycleMap_apply, weilDivisorEquivFinsupp_cartierWeilDivisor,
    Finsupp.ofSupportFinite_coe]
  have h := isOrderAlong_orderAlong hX ((codim1SubvarietyEquivPrimeDivisor k hX).symm P) τ
  rw [coe_codim1SubvarietyEquivPrimeDivisor_symm_apply] at h
  exact cartierMultiplicity_eq_of_isOrderAlong h

include k hX in
/-- The Stacks Weil divisor `[τ]` of a Cartier divisor is a Weil divisor of `τ` in the sense of
orders along prime divisors. -/
private theorem isWeilDivisorOfCartier_cartierWeilDivisor [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [NoetherianSpace X] (τ : X.CartierDivisor) :
    letI : IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
    IsWeilDivisorOfCartier τ (weilDivisorEquivFinsupp (cartierWeilDivisor τ)) := by
  letI : IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
  intro P
  have h := isOrderAlong_orderAlong hX ((codim1SubvarietyEquivPrimeDivisor k hX).symm P) τ
  rw [coe_codim1SubvarietyEquivPrimeDivisor_symm_apply] at h
  change IsOrderAlong τ _ (weilDivisorEquivFinsupp (cartierWeilDivisor τ) P)
  rwa [weilDivisorEquivFinsupp_cartierWeilDivisor, Finsupp.ofSupportFinite_coe,
    cartierMultiplicity_eq_of_isOrderAlong h]

end CartierWeil

open MMP.Intersection in
/-- A smooth variety over a field has pure dimension `n` for some `n : ℕ`. -/
private theorem exists_isPureDimensional (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsSmoothVariety k f] [CompactSpace X] :
    ∃ n : ℕ, IsPureDimensional X n := by
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ : ∃ n : ℕ, topologicalKrullDim X = n := by
    have h1 := topologicalKrullDim_ne_top_of_locallyOfFiniteType k f
    have h0 : topologicalKrullDim X ≠ ⊥ := (Order.krullDim_ne_bot_iff
      (α := IrreducibleCloseds X)).mpr ⟨IrreducibleCloseds.closureSingleton (Classical.arbitrary X)⟩
    obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := WithBot.ne_bot_iff_exists.mp h0
    have hd' : d ≠ ⊤ := by rintro rfl; exact h1 hd.symm
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := ENat.ne_top_iff_exists.mp hd'
    exact ⟨m, by rw [← hd, ← hm]; rfl⟩
  refine ⟨n, fun Z hZ => ?_⟩
  rw [irreducibleComponents_eq_singleton] at hZ
  rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp hZ, (Homeomorph.Set.univ X).isHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq]
  exact hn

open MMP.Intersection in
/-- The Weil divisor map `τ ↦ [τ]` on Cartier divisors of a smooth variety is bijective
(Hartshorne II.6.11). -/
private theorem cartierWeil_bijective (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsSmoothVariety k f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [CompactSpace X] [IsNormal X] :
    letI : IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
    Function.Bijective (fun τ : X.CartierDivisor =>
      (weilDivisorEquivFinsupp (cartierWeilDivisor τ) : Divisor X)) := by
  letI : IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
  letI : X.Over (Spec (.of k)) := ⟨f⟩
  have hsm : IsSmoothScheme f := isSmoothScheme_of_smooth inferInstance
  haveI : LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) := inferInstanceAs (LocallyOfFiniteType f)
  obtain ⟨n, hX⟩ := exists_isPureDimensional k f
  have key : (fun τ : X.CartierDivisor =>
      (weilDivisorEquivFinsupp (cartierWeilDivisor τ) : Divisor X)) =
      Finsupp.domCongr (codim1SubvarietyEquivPrimeDivisor k hX) ∘ cycleMap hX :=
    funext (weilDivisorEquivFinsupp_cartierWeilDivisor_eq k hX)
  rw [key]
  exact (Finsupp.domCongr _).bijective.comp
    (cycleMap_bijective_of_uniqueFactorizationMonoid k hX fun _ =>
      uniqueFactorizationMonoid_stalk_of_mem_smoothLocus (by rw [hsm]; trivial))

section DivisorialLineBundle

open MMP.Intersection

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X]

private theorem bijective_stalkSpecializes_of_eq_genericPoint {x : X} (h : genericPoint X ⤳ x)
    (hx : x = genericPoint X) : Function.Bijective (X.presheaf.stalkSpecializes h).hom := by
  subst hx
  rw [TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes_refl]
  exact Function.bijective_id

/-- The factor `𝒪_{X,η_Z}` of `K(X)` is the function field. -/
private noncomputable def componentStalkEquiv (Z : irreducibleComponents X) :
    X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z) ≃+* X.functionField :=
  RingEquiv.ofBijective
    (X.presheaf.stalkSpecializes ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial)).hom
    (bijective_stalkSpecializes_of_eq_genericPoint _
      (MMP.Fourfold.componentGenericPoint_eq_genericPoint Z))

private theorem componentStalkEquiv_apply (Z : irreducibleComponents X)
    (a : X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint X Z)) :
    componentStalkEquiv Z a = algebraMap _ X.functionField a := rfl

/-- The value in `K(X)` of a section of `𝓜_X` at a point. -/
private noncomputable def rationalValue (V : X.Opens) (σ : X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op V))
    (x : X) (hx : x ∈ V) : X.functionField :=
  totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField x (X.totalQuotientSheaf.presheaf.germ V x hx σ)

private theorem rationalValue_eq_generic (V : X.Opens) (σ : X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op V))
    (x : X) (hx : x ∈ V) :
    rationalValue V σ x hx = rationalValue V σ (genericPoint X)
      (((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial : genericPoint X ⤳ x).mem_open V.isOpen hx) := by
  have h : genericPoint X ⤳ x := (genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial
  unfold rationalValue
  rw [← totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField_stalkSpecializes h]
  congr 1
  exact TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes_apply _ _ _ _

private theorem rationalValue_eq (V : X.Opens) (σ : X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op V)) {x y : X}
    (hx : x ∈ V) (hy : y ∈ V) : rationalValue V σ x hx = rationalValue V σ y hy := by
  rw [rationalValue_eq_generic, rationalValue_eq_generic V σ y]

private theorem rationalValue_res {U V : X.Opens} (i : V ⟶ U)
    (σ : X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op U)) (x : X) (hx : x ∈ V) :
    rationalValue V (X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.map i.op σ) x hx = rationalValue U σ x (i.le hx) := by
  unfold rationalValue
  rw [TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply]

/-- A rational function is a section of `𝓜_X` over every open. -/
private theorem exists_rationalValue_eq (V : X.Opens) (φ : X.functionField) :
    ∃ σ : X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op V), ∀ x hx, rationalValue V σ x hx = φ := by
  choose m hm using fun x : V => (totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField_bijective x.1).2 φ
  choose W hxW s hs using fun x : V => X.totalQuotientSheaf.presheaf.germ_exist (x := x.1) (m x)
  let W' : V → X.Opens := fun x => W x ⊓ V
  let s' : ∀ x, X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op (W' x)) := fun x =>
    X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left : W' x ≤ W x)).op (s x)
  have hs' : ∀ x z (hz : z ∈ W' x), rationalValue (W' x) (s' x) z hz = φ := by
    intro x z hz
    rw [rationalValue_eq _ _ hz (show x.1 ∈ W' x from ⟨hxW x, x.2⟩)]
    unfold rationalValue s'
    rw [TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply, hs x, hm x]
  have hcompat : TopCat.Presheaf.IsCompatible X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj W' s' := by
    intro x y
    apply TopCat.Presheaf.section_ext X.totalQuotientSheaf
    intro z hz
    apply (totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField_bijective z).1
    have h1 := rationalValue_res (homOfLE (inf_le_left : W' x ⊓ W' y ≤ W' x)) (s' x) z hz
    have h2 := rationalValue_res (homOfLE (inf_le_right : W' x ⊓ W' y ≤ W' y)) (s' y) z hz
    exact h1.trans ((hs' x z hz.1).trans ((hs' y z hz.2).symm.trans h2.symm))
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ, -⟩ := X.totalQuotientSheaf.existsUnique_gluing' W' V
    (fun x => homOfLE inf_le_right)
    (fun x hx => Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, hxW _, hx⟩) s' hcompat
  refine ⟨σ, fun x hx => ?_⟩
  have h1 := hs' ⟨x, hx⟩ x ⟨hxW _, hx⟩
  have h2 := rationalValue_res (homOfLE (inf_le_right : W' ⟨x, hx⟩ ≤ V)) σ x ⟨hxW _, hx⟩
  rw [hσ ⟨x, hx⟩] at h2
  exact h2.symm.trans h1

/-- A section of `𝓜_X` read as a section of `𝒦_X`. -/
private noncomputable def toRationalSection (V : X.Opens)
    (σ : X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op V)) :
    ToType ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op V)) :=
  fun Z => (componentStalkEquiv Z.1).symm (rationalValue V σ _ Z.2)

private theorem componentStalkEquiv_toRationalSection (V : X.Opens)
    (σ : X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op V))
    (Z : {Z : irreducibleComponents X // componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ V}) :
    componentStalkEquiv Z.1 (toRationalSection V σ Z) = rationalValue V σ _ Z.2 :=
  (componentStalkEquiv Z.1).apply_symm_apply _

private theorem toRationalSection_injective (V : X.Opens) :
    Function.Injective (toRationalSection V) := by
  intro σ σ' h
  apply TopCat.Presheaf.section_ext X.totalQuotientSheaf
  intro x hx
  apply (totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField_bijective x).1
  obtain ⟨Z, -⟩ := exists_mem_irreducibleComponents x
  have hZ : componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ V := by
    rw [MMP.Fourfold.componentGenericPoint_eq_genericPoint]
    exact ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial : genericPoint X ⤳ x).mem_open V.isOpen hx
  change rationalValue V σ x hx = rationalValue V σ' x hx
  rw [rationalValue_eq V σ hx hZ, rationalValue_eq V σ' hx hZ,
    ← componentStalkEquiv_toRationalSection V σ ⟨Z, hZ⟩,
    ← componentStalkEquiv_toRationalSection V σ' ⟨Z, hZ⟩, h]

private theorem toRationalSection_res {U V : X.Opens} (i : V ⟶ U)
    (σ : X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op U)) :
    toRationalSection V (X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.map i.op σ) =
      (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).map i.op (toRationalSection U σ) := by
  funext Z
  rw [rationalFunctionsPresheaf_map_apply]
  simp only [toRationalSection, rationalValue_res]

private theorem toRationalSection_add (V : X.Opens) (σ σ' : X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op V)) :
    toRationalSection V (σ + σ') = toRationalSection V σ + toRationalSection V σ' := by
  funext Z
  change _ = toRationalSection V σ Z + toRationalSection V σ' Z
  simp only [toRationalSection, rationalValue, map_add]

private theorem toRationalSection_smul (V : X.Opens) (r : Γ(X, V))
    (σ : X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op V)) :
    toRationalSection V (r • σ) = r • toRationalSection V σ := by
  funext Z
  rw [rationalFunctions_smul_apply]
  apply (componentStalkEquiv Z.1).injective
  rw [componentStalkEquiv_toRationalSection, map_mul, componentStalkEquiv_toRationalSection,
    smul_totalQuotient_def]
  unfold rationalValue
  rw [map_mul, map_mul, germ_toTotalQuotient,
    totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField_stalkToTotalQuotient, componentStalkEquiv_apply]

variable [IsNormal X]

/-- A nonzero rational function as a unit of `K(X)`. -/
private noncomputable def unitOfNeZero {φ : X.functionField} (hφ : φ ≠ 0) :
    (RationalFunctions X)ˣ :=
  (RationalFunctions.unitsEquiv X).symm fun Z =>
    Units.map (componentStalkEquiv Z).symm.toMonoidHom (Units.mk0 φ hφ)

private theorem coe_unitOfNeZero_apply {φ : X.functionField} (hφ : φ ≠ 0)
    (Z : irreducibleComponents X) :
    (unitOfNeZero hφ : RationalFunctions X) Z = (componentStalkEquiv Z).symm φ := rfl

private theorem valuation_componentStalkEquiv_symm (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)
    {φ : X.functionField} (hφ : φ ≠ 0) :
    E.valuation ((componentStalkEquiv E.component).symm φ) =
      WithZero.exp (X.ord φ E.genericPoint) := by
  rw [← coe_unitOfNeZero_apply hφ, E.valuation_component,
    MMP.Positivity.ord_eq_ord_componentToFunctionField]
  congr 2
  exact (componentStalkEquiv E.component).apply_symm_apply φ

private theorem mem_lineBundleSections_iff_isDivisorialSection {G : X.CartierDivisor}
    {w : Divisor X} (hG : IsWeilDivisorOfCartier G w) (V : X.Opens)
    (σ : X.totalQuotientSheaf.obj.obj (op V)) :
    σ ∈ lineBundleSections G V ↔ w.IsDivisorialSection V (toRationalSection V σ) := by
  by_cases hV : (V : Set X).Nonempty
  · obtain ⟨x₀, hx₀⟩ := hV
    haveI : Nonempty V := ⟨⟨x₀, hx₀⟩⟩
    set φ := rationalValue V σ x₀ hx₀
    have hval : ∀ x (hx : x ∈ V), rationalValue V σ x hx = φ := fun x hx =>
      rationalValue_eq V σ hx hx₀
    have hchi : ∀ Z, toRationalSection V σ Z = (componentStalkEquiv Z.1).symm φ := fun Z => by
      simp only [toRationalSection, hval]
    by_cases hφ : φ = 0
    · constructor
      · intro _ E _
        left
        rw [hchi, hφ, map_zero]
      · intro _ x hx f _
        have h0 : X.totalQuotientSheaf.presheaf.germ V x hx σ = 0 :=
          (totalQuotientStalkToFunctionField_bijective x).1
            (by rw [map_zero]; exact (hval x hx).trans hφ)
        rw [h0, zero_mul]
        exact zero_mem _
    · rw [mem_lineBundleSections_iff_forall_zero_le_ord_add hG V hφ σ hval]
      refine forall_congr' fun E => forall_congr' fun hE => ?_
      rw [PrimeDivisor.OrdGE, hchi]
      have hne : (componentStalkEquiv E.component).symm φ ≠ 0 := by
        rw [Ne, map_eq_zero_iff _ (componentStalkEquiv E.component).symm.injective]
        exact hφ
      rw [or_iff_right hne, valuation_componentStalkEquiv_symm E hφ, WithZero.exp_le_exp]
      constructor <;> intro h <;> linarith
  · rw [Set.not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty] at hV
    constructor
    · intro _ E hE
      exact absurd hE (by rw [hV, Set.inter_empty]; exact Set.not_nonempty_empty)
    · intro _ x hx
      exact absurd (show x ∈ (V : Set X) from hx) (by rw [hV]; exact id)

variable {G : X.CartierDivisor} {w : Divisor X}

private theorem toRationalSection_surjective (hG : IsWeilDivisorOfCartier G w) (V : X.Opens)
    (ψ : w.divisorialSubmodule V) :
    ∃ σ : lineBundleSections G V, toRationalSection V σ.1 = ψ.1 := by
  by_cases hV : ∃ Z : irreducibleComponents X, componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ V
  · obtain ⟨Z₀, hZ₀⟩ := hV
    obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := exists_rationalValue_eq V (componentStalkEquiv Z₀ (ψ.1 ⟨Z₀, hZ₀⟩))
    have hchi : toRationalSection V σ = ψ.1 := by
      funext Z
      apply (componentStalkEquiv Z.1).injective
      rw [componentStalkEquiv_toRationalSection, hσ]
      obtain rfl : Z = ⟨Z₀, hZ₀⟩ := Subtype.ext <| Subtype.ext <|
        (MMP.Threefold.Mori.CanonUniq.component_eq_univ _).trans
          (MMP.Threefold.Mori.CanonUniq.component_eq_univ _).symm
      rfl
    exact ⟨⟨σ, (mem_lineBundleSections_iff_isDivisorialSection hG V σ).2 (hchi ▸ ψ.2)⟩, hchi⟩
  · simp only [not_exists] at hV
    exact ⟨0, funext fun Z => absurd Z.2 (hV Z.1)⟩

/-- The map `𝒪_X(G)(V) → 𝒪_X([G])(V)`, reading a section of `𝓜_X` in `𝒦_X`. -/
private noncomputable def toRationalSectionLinear (hG : IsWeilDivisorOfCartier G w) (V : X.Opens) :
    Γ(MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf G, V) →ₗ[Γ(X, V)] w.divisorialSubmodule V where
  toFun σ := ⟨toRationalSection V (MMP.CartierDivisorSheaf.sectionVal σ),
    (mem_lineBundleSections_iff_isDivisorialSection hG V _).1
      (MMP.CartierDivisor.sectionVal_mem_lineBundleSections σ)⟩
  map_add' σ σ' := Subtype.ext (toRationalSection_add V _ _)
  map_smul' r σ := Subtype.ext (toRationalSection_smul V r _)

/-- The morphism `𝒪_X(G) ⟶ 𝒪_X([G])`. -/
private noncomputable def lineBundleToDivisorialSheaf (hG : IsWeilDivisorOfCartier G w) :
    MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf G ⟶ w.divisorialSheaf :=
  ⟨PresheafOfModules.homMk
    { app U := AddCommGrpCat.ofHom (toRationalSectionLinear hG U.unop).toAddMonoidHom
      naturality U V i := by
        ext σ
        exact Subtype.ext
          (toRationalSection_res i.unop (MMP.CartierDivisorSheaf.sectionVal σ)) }
    fun U r t => (toRationalSectionLinear hG U.unop).map_smul r t⟩

private theorem isIso_lineBundleToDivisorialSheaf (hG : IsWeilDivisorOfCartier G w) :
    IsIso (lineBundleToDivisorialSheaf hG) := by
  rw [Scheme.Modules.Hom.isIso_iff_isIso_app]
  intro U
  rw [ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective]
  refine ⟨fun t t' h => Subtype.ext (toRationalSection_injective U (congrArg Subtype.val h)),
    fun f => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := toRationalSection_surjective hG U f
  exact ⟨MMP.CartierDivisor.sectionOfMem t.2, Subtype.ext ht⟩

end DivisorialLineBundle

/-- On a smooth variety the divisorial sheaf of `[τ]` is the invertible sheaf of `τ`. -/
private theorem divisorialSheaf_cartierWeil_iso (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsSmoothVariety k f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [CompactSpace X] [IsNormal X] :
    letI : IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
    ∀ τ : X.CartierDivisor,
      Nonempty (Divisor.divisorialSheaf (weilDivisorEquivFinsupp (cartierWeilDivisor τ)) ≅
        MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf τ) := by
  letI : IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
  letI : X.Over (Spec (.of k)) := ⟨f⟩
  haveI : LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) := inferInstanceAs (LocallyOfFiniteType f)
  obtain ⟨n, hX⟩ := exists_isPureDimensional k f
  intro τ
  have hG := isWeilDivisorOfCartier_cartierWeilDivisor k hX τ
  exact ⟨(@asIso _ _ _ _ (lineBundleToDivisorialSheaf hG)
    (isIso_lineBundleToDivisorialSheaf hG)).symm⟩

/-- On a smooth variety every invertible sheaf is a divisorial sheaf (Hartshorne II.6.16). -/
private theorem exists_divisorialSheaf_iso_of_isInvertibleModule (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsSmoothVariety k f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [CompactSpace X] [IsNormal X] :
    ∀ L : X.Modules, Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L →
      ∃ B : Divisor X, Nonempty (Divisor.divisorialSheaf B ≅ L) := by
  intro L hL
  haveI := hL
  have : ∀ z : X.toRingedSpace.carrier,
      IsLocalRing (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.ringStalk X.toRingedSpace z) :=
    X.isLocalRing
  choose W hW a ha using fun y : X =>
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_bijective_smul_of_isInvertible (X := X.toRingedSpace) L y
  obtain ⟨y₀⟩ : Nonempty X := inferInstance
  exact MMP.Mori.LocalFrame.exists_divisorialSheaf_iso
    { W := W, mem := hW, a := a, isLocalGenerator := ha, base := y₀ }

/-- **Divisors and invertible sheaves on a smooth variety.** On a smooth variety `X` over a
field: every Weil divisor is Cartier; the ideal of a prime divisor `P` is generated, on an affine
neighbourhood of each point, by a regular function `g` which is a local equation of `P`; the
Weil divisor of a Cartier divisor `τ` defines a bijection `τ ↦ [τ]` with
`𝒪_X([τ]) ≅ 𝒪_X(τ)`; every invertible sheaf is `𝒪_X(B)` for some divisor `B`; and every
`ℚ`-divisor is `ℚ`-Cartier. -/
@[mmp "lem_mmp_threefold_smooth_divisor_line_bundle_dictionary"]
public theorem Divisor.cartier_weil_dictionary_of_isSmoothVariety (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [hf : IsSmoothVariety k f] :
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian X :=
      @LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian _ _ f hf.toLocallyOfFiniteType
        (isLocallyNoetherian_Spec.mpr inferInstance)
    letI : CompactSpace X :=
      @QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace _ _ f hf.toQuasiCompact PrimeSpectrum.compactSpace
    letI : IsNormal X := @isNormal_of_smooth_over_field k _ X f hf.toSmooth
    (∀ D : Divisor X, Divisor.IsCartier D) ∧
    (∀ (P : PrimeDivisor X) (x : X), ∃ U : X.affineOpens, x ∈ (U : X.Opens) ∧
      ∃ (g : Γ(X, U)) (φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ),
        (∀ (Z : irreducibleComponents X) (hZ : componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ (U : X.Opens)),
          (φ : RationalFunctions X) Z = X.presheaf.germ U _ hZ g) ∧
        Divisor.IsLocalEquation (Finsupp.single P 1) U φ ∧
        P.idealSheaf.ideal U = Ideal.span {g}) ∧
    letI : IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
    Function.Bijective (fun τ : X.CartierDivisor =>
      (weilDivisorEquivFinsupp (cartierWeilDivisor τ) : Divisor X)) ∧
    (∀ τ : X.CartierDivisor,
      Nonempty (Divisor.divisorialSheaf (weilDivisorEquivFinsupp (cartierWeilDivisor τ)) ≅
        MMP.CartierDivisor.sheaf τ)) ∧
    (∀ L : X.Modules, Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L →
      ∃ B : Divisor X, Nonempty (Divisor.divisorialSheaf B ≅ L)) ∧
    (∀ D : QDivisor X, QDivisor.IsQCartier D) := by
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian X :=
    @LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian _ _ f hf.toLocallyOfFiniteType
      (isLocallyNoetherian_Spec.mpr inferInstance)
  let : CompactSpace X :=
    @QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace _ _ f hf.toQuasiCompact PrimeSpectrum.compactSpace
  let : IsNormal X := @isNormal_of_smooth_over_field k _ X f hf.toSmooth
  have hsm : IsSmoothScheme f := isSmoothScheme_of_smooth hf.toSmooth
  exact ⟨MMP.Fourfold.isCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsm,
    exists_affine_ideal_eq_span_isLocalEquation k hsm,
    cartierWeil_bijective k f, divisorialSheaf_cartierWeil_iso k f,
    exists_divisorialSheaf_iso_of_isInvertibleModule k f,
    MMP.Fourfold.isQCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsm⟩

end SmoothVariety

section SmoothPoint

open TopologicalSpace Order Topology MMP.Intersection

section

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

section Divisor

variable [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]

/-- On an integral normal scheme, a prime divisor `E` has a local equation near every point
whose local ring is factorial. -/
private theorem exists_isLocalEquation_single [IsIntegral X] [NoetherianSpace X] {P : X}
    (hUFD : UniqueFactorizationMonoid (X.presheaf.stalk P)) (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) :
    ∃ U : X.Opens, P ∈ U ∧ ∃ φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ,
      Divisor.IsLocalEquation (Finsupp.single E 1 : Divisor X) U φ := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨U, s, hPU, hs0, hord, hmax⟩ := exists_section_ord_eq_ite E.coheight_genericPoint P hUFD
  have hmem : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents X, componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U := fun Z => by
    rw [genericPoint_mem_iff]
    exact ⟨P, hPU, Z.2.2 (IrreducibleSpace.isIrreducible_univ X) (Set.subset_univ _) trivial⟩
  have hunit : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents X,
      IsUnit (X.presheaf.germ U _ (hmem Z) s) := fun Z => by
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := (RationalFunctions.isField_stalk X Z).mul_inv_cancel (hs0 _ (hmem Z))
    exact ⟨⟨_, b, hb, by rwa [mul_comm]⟩, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨U, hPU, (Pi.isUnit_iff.2 hunit).unit, fun F hF => ?_⟩
  have hFU := F.genericPoint_mem_of_nonempty hF
  have hφ : F.toComponent.hom (X.presheaf.germ U _ hFU s) =
      ((Pi.isUnit_iff.2 hunit).unit : RationalFunctions X) F.component :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes_apply _ _ _ _
  rw [DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
  by_cases hFE : F = E
  · subst hFE
    rw [if_pos rfl]
    have := F.isDiscreteValuationRing_localRing
    exact (F.ord_eq_one_of_irreducible
      ((IsDiscreteValuationRing.irreducible_iff_uniformizer _).2 (hmax hFU)) hφ).symm
  · rw [if_neg (Ne.symm hFE)]
    exact (F.ord_eq_zero_of_isUnit (isUnit_of_ord_eq_zero
      ((hord _ hFU F.coheight_genericPoint.le).trans (if_neg fun e =>
        hFE (AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.genericPoint_injective e)))) hφ).symm

/-- On an integral normal Noetherian scheme every Weil divisor has a local equation near every
point whose local ring is factorial. -/
private theorem exists_isLocalEquation_of_uniqueFactorizationMonoid [IsIntegral X]
    [NoetherianSpace X] {P : X} (hUFD : UniqueFactorizationMonoid (X.presheaf.stalk P))
    (D : Divisor X) :
    ∃ U : X.Opens, P ∈ U ∧ ∃ φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ, D.IsLocalEquation U φ := by
  induction D using Finsupp.induction_linear with
  | zero => exact ⟨⊤, trivial, 1, Divisor.isLocalEquation_zero ⊤⟩
  | add D D' hD hD' =>
    obtain ⟨U, hU, φ, hφ⟩ := hD
    obtain ⟨U', hU', φ', hφ'⟩ := hD'
    exact ⟨U ⊓ U', ⟨hU, hU'⟩, φ * φ', (hφ.mono inf_le_left).add (hφ'.mono inf_le_right)⟩
  | single E c =>
    obtain ⟨U, hU, φ, hφ⟩ := exists_isLocalEquation_single hUFD E
    refine ⟨U, hU, φ ^ c, fun F hF => ?_⟩
    classical
    rw [PrimeDivisor.ord_zpow, ← hφ F hF]
    rw [DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_apply, DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_apply, Finsupp.single_apply,
      Finsupp.single_apply]
    split_ifs <;> simp

end Divisor

end

/-- **Weil divisors are Cartier near a smooth point of a normal surface.** If `X` is a normal
surface over `k` and `P` lies in the smooth locus of `X`, then every Weil divisor `D` has a local
equation `φ ∈ K(X)^*` on some open neighbourhood `U` of `P`; and for every `ℚ`-divisor `D` there
are an open neighbourhood `U` of `P` and a positive integer `m` such that `m • D` is an integral
divisor having a local equation on `U`. -/
@[mmp "lem_mmp_threefold_surface_smooth_weil_cartier"]
public theorem Divisor.exists_isLocalEquation_of_mem_smoothLocus (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    (hX : IsNormalVariety k f) (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X = 2)
    {P : X} (hP : P ∈ smoothLocus f) :
    (∀ D : Divisor X,
      ∃ U : X.Opens, P ∈ U ∧ ∃ φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ, D.IsLocalEquation U φ) ∧
    (∀ D : QDivisor X,
      ∃ U : X.Opens, P ∈ U ∧ ∃ m : ℕ, 0 < m ∧ ∃ D' : Divisor X,
        Divisor.toQDivisor D' = (m : ℤ) • D ∧
        ∃ φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ, D'.IsLocalEquation U φ) := by
  have : IsIntegral X := hX.1.toIsIntegral
  have : QuasiCompact f := hX.1.toQuasiCompact
  have : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace f
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.IsNoetherian X := ⟨⟩
  have h1 := exists_isLocalEquation_of_uniqueFactorizationMonoid
    (uniqueFactorizationMonoid_stalk_of_mem_smoothLocus hP)
  refine ⟨h1, fun D => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨m, hm0, D', hD'⟩ := MMP.Flips.exists_pos_smul_eq_toQDivisor D
  obtain ⟨U, hU, φ, hφ⟩ := h1 D'
  exact ⟨U, hU, m, hm0, D', hD', φ, hφ⟩

end SmoothPoint

end MMP.Mori
